select-sym-def-object-camellia: Camellia storage parents select their symmetric definition

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Library, Part 1, "Symmetric Encryption" (Protected
Storage)):

  "The block cipher used for encrypting the object's sensitive area is the
  symmetric cipher of the Storage Parent."

CryptoCommon_SelectSymDefObject() switches on the algorithm ID of the
parent's symmetric definition, but its SM4 and Camellia case labels are the
ALG_SM4/ALG_CAMELLIA profile switches (value 1) instead of TPM_ALG_SM4 and
TPM_ALG_CAMELLIA, so every RSA, ECC or SYMCIPHER parent whose symmetric
algorithm is Camellia reaches FAIL_BOOL(FATAL_ERROR_INTERNAL): TPM2_Create,
TPM2_Load, TPM2_Import, TPM2_MakeCredential/TPM2_ActivateCredential and the
other users of the parent's symmetric definition put the TPM into failure mode
instead of protecting the object with Camellia.

diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/cryptolibs/common/CryptUtil.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/cryptolibs/common/CryptUtil.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/cryptolibs/common/CryptUtil.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/cryptolibs/common/CryptUtil.c
@@ -1375,13 +1375,17 @@
             symDefObject->keyBits.aes = objectSym->keyBits.aes;
             break;
 #endif  // ALG_AES
+        // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT
+        // determinism): the case labels are the algorithm IDs TPM_ALG_SM4 and
+        // TPM_ALG_CAMELLIA, not the ALG_SM4/ALG_CAMELLIA profile switches (1),
+        // which sent every SM4/Camellia parent to the FAIL below.
 #if ALG_SM4
-        case ALG_SM4:
+        case TPM_ALG_SM4:
             symDefObject->keyBits.sm4 = objectSym->keyBits.sm4;
             break;
 #endif  // ALG_SM2
 #if ALG_CAMELLIA
-        case ALG_CAMELLIA:
+        case TPM_ALG_CAMELLIA:
             symDefObject->keyBits.camellia = objectSym->keyBits.camellia;
             break;
 #endif  // ALG_SM2
